---
globs:
  - "src/**/*.ts"
---

Failures raised in `src/` are `AppError` from `src/errors/appError.ts` or a subclass (`WebhookParseError`, `StaleHeadPushError`), with a stable `code` shaped `<domain>.<reason_snake>` (`config.invalid_enum`, `ask.sensitive_path_blocked`, `triage.stale_head_push`), a technical `message`, JSON-safe `context` (never secrets or repo content), and `cause` when wrapping. Callers branch on `code` or `instanceof`, never on message text. `AppError.message` and `context` never reach a PR comment, check, reaction, or status; PR-facing copy is a plain-English settings constant. Log with `errorLogFields` / `serializeAppError`; `sanitizeErrorForTelemetry` guards evlog and analytics. `throw new Error(...)` is only for programmer invariants no caller branches on (`src/agent/execution/json.ts`, `src/util/uuidv5.ts`); a failure that retry, executor, or intake code can observe gets an `AppError`. Retry classification is `classifyFailure` in `src/errors/classifiedFailure.ts`.
